The addresses om hands out in this network, as a subnet of the segment the
nodes share, as `fd01:2345:6789:4599::1:0/112` in `fd01:2345:6789:4599::/64`.

Every node draws from the whole of it, so an address is the same wherever the
object runs, and an object moving to another node takes its address along.
Keep it clear of the addresses of the nodes and of the other hosts of the
segment: om hands out every address of it but the first.
